<http://data.silknow.org/object/9df87378-37c2-34b0-b7b8-71d0a9c549cc>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "The line borders, narrow rectangular shape, and non-reversible stitching indicate that this textile was originally lined and used as a pillow or bolster cover. The palette and airy design suggest it was made in the late 18th or early 19th century. \nThis example is embellished in atma stitching—a particularly labor- and material-intensive technique most commonly found in Ottoman textiles of the late 17th to late 18th centuries." , "Ottoman Turkish Interior Textiles from the Aldrich Collection" , "January 22 - July 17, 2016" ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/78d2ffd3-ebb4-33ab-8424-9b7813b07382> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    "Exhibition" ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Ottoman Turkish Interior Textiles from the Aldrich Collection" , "January 22 - July 17, 2016" , "The line borders, narrow rectangular shape, and non-reversible stitching indicate that this textile was originally lined and used as a pillow or bolster cover. The palette and airy design suggest it was made in the late 18th or early 19th century. \nThis example is embellished in atma stitching—a particularly labor- and material-intensive technique most commonly found in Ottoman textiles of the late 17th to late 18th centuries." ;
        schema:contentUrl   <https://risdmuseum.org/exhibitions-events/exhibitions/ottoman-turkish-interior-textiles-aldrich-collection> .

